  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering waste pickers to create an alternative urban waste management system</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The area of Tema New Town in Ghana has no organized waste collection due to inhabitants&#x2019; inability to pay. Therefore, waste is dumped along the coastal line or burned. Environment360 founded a Pick-it sorting centre in Tema New Town to improve livelihoods of waste pickers and support an alternative waste collection system that supports Ghana&#x2019;s Nationally Determined Contributions. The project strengthened the capacity of more than 300 waste pickers in Tema New Town and surrounding areas to scale their businesses and independently operate at the Pick-It facility. This action increased the overall volume of recycled plastic, to reduce plastic that is illegally disposed or burned.</narrative>
  </description>
